1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,820
A content item needs a name you can recognize.

2
00:00:03,820 --> 00:00:07,669
The Title part gives a content type a title that an editor types,

3
00:00:07,669 --> 00:00:10,272
or that the site builds from other fields.

4
00:00:10,272 --> 00:00:14,610
Let's add the part, try its behaviors, and generate titles from a pattern.

5
00:00:19,210 --> 00:00:23,412
A content type describes a kind of content, such as a product, and

6
00:00:23,412 --> 00:00:26,330
each content item is one entry of that type.

7
00:00:26,330 --> 00:00:30,241
A content item can have a display text, which is the name the

8
00:00:30,241 --> 00:00:32,050
admin shows in its lists.

9
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:36,733
An item without a display text is listed under the name of its

10
00:00:36,733 --> 00:00:40,724
content type, which makes items of one type hard to tell apart.

11
00:00:40,724 --> 00:00:45,640
The Title part gives a content type a title, and stores it as the display text.

12
00:00:46,390 --> 00:00:50,214
An editor can type the title, or the site can generate it from

13
00:00:50,214 --> 00:00:51,958
other fields of the item.

14
00:00:51,958 --> 00:00:55,670
A Behavior option on the part chooses between four settings:

15
00:00:55,670 --> 00:01:01,800
editable, editable and required, generated with the input disabled, or generated with the input hidden.

16
00:01:06,023 --> 00:01:11,511
Under Design, Content Definition, Content Types, you find every content type of the site.

17
00:01:11,511 --> 00:01:14,399
Product has two Text fields, Brand and Name.

18
00:01:14,399 --> 00:01:16,363
Let's click Edit on Product.

19
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:20,366
Add Parts lists the parts that you can attach to a type.

20
00:01:20,366 --> 00:01:21,910
Title is one of them.

21
00:01:21,910 --> 00:01:25,170
Add & Configure attaches it and opens its settings.

22
00:01:25,626 --> 00:01:27,633
The settings of the part open.

23
00:01:27,633 --> 00:01:31,479
The Behavior option is Title is editable, which is the default.

24
00:01:31,479 --> 00:01:35,826
Render Title is checked, so the part renders the title in display views.

25
00:01:36,277 --> 00:01:39,964
Placeholder sets the hint text of an empty Title field.

26
00:01:39,964 --> 00:01:45,827
Let's type Product title, and choose Title is editable and required as the Behavior option.

27
00:01:46,286 --> 00:01:49,885
Save stores the settings on the Product type, and a message confirms that

28
00:01:49,885 --> 00:01:51,706
the part settings have been saved.

29
00:01:55,897 --> 00:02:00,703
On the Content Types page, Create New Product opens the editor for a product.

30
00:02:00,703 --> 00:02:04,467
It has a Title field, and the placeholder text shows in it.

31
00:02:04,932 --> 00:02:07,740
Let's publish with the Title field empty.

32
00:02:07,740 --> 00:02:11,923
The title is required, so the item is not saved, and the message

33
00:02:11,923 --> 00:02:14,432
reads A value is required for Title.

34
00:02:14,888 --> 00:02:19,190
Let's type Brightwater Camp Stove in the Title field and publish.

35
00:02:19,190 --> 00:02:23,068
The item is saved, and the Content Types page opens again.

36
00:02:23,525 --> 00:02:26,997
List Items on the Product row shows its content items.

37
00:02:26,997 --> 00:02:30,585
The title you typed is the name of the item in the list.

38
00:02:34,808 --> 00:02:39,966
To generate titles, let's edit Product again and then edit the Title part.

39
00:02:39,966 --> 00:02:45,318
Let's choose Title is generated and input is disabled as the Behavior option.

40
00:02:45,776 --> 00:02:47,481
The Pattern field appears.

41
00:02:47,481 --> 00:02:50,837
It takes a template that can read the fields of the item.

42
00:02:50,837 --> 00:02:55,206
Let's combine the Brand field and the Name field, with a space between them.

43
00:02:55,661 --> 00:03:00,276
The editor cannot type in a generated title, so let's clear the Placeholder.

44
00:03:00,276 --> 00:03:02,021
Save stores the settings.

45
00:03:02,473 --> 00:03:06,721
On the Content Types page, Create New Product opens the editor with the

46
00:03:06,721 --> 00:03:11,963
Title field disabled, and a hint says The title will be auto-generated using the pattern.

47
00:03:11,963 --> 00:03:16,873
Let's fill in Brightwater as the Brand and Trail Backpack as the Name, and publish.

48
00:03:17,334 --> 00:03:21,396
List Items shows the item named Brightwater Trail Backpack.

49
00:03:21,396 --> 00:03:26,334
The site builds the title again each time the item is saved or published.

50
00:03:26,794 --> 00:03:29,235
Edit opens the item in the editor.

51
00:03:29,235 --> 00:03:33,324
The Title field holds the generated title and stays disabled.

52
00:03:33,786 --> 00:03:37,800
Back on the list, View opens the item on the site in a new tab.

53
00:03:37,800 --> 00:03:40,766
The heading of the page shows the same title.

54
00:03:44,967 --> 00:03:47,256
The last option hides the field.

55
00:03:47,256 --> 00:03:52,978
Let's edit the Title part again, choose Title is generated and input is hidden, and save.

56
00:03:52,978 --> 00:03:55,387
The same pattern builds the title.

57
00:03:55,839 --> 00:04:00,712
Back on the Content Types page, Create New Product shows no Title field at all.

58
00:04:00,712 --> 00:04:05,699
Let's fill in Brightwater as the Brand and Water Bottle as the Name, and publish.

59
00:04:06,156 --> 00:04:08,876
List Items shows Brightwater Water Bottle.

60
00:04:08,876 --> 00:04:14,146
Whichever option you choose, the title ends up as the display text of the content item.

61
00:04:16,146 --> 00:04:18,748
The Title part names your content items:

62
00:04:18,748 --> 00:04:23,895
editors type the title, or a pattern generates it, with the field disabled or hidden.

63
00:04:23,895 --> 00:04:25,366
Thanks for watching.

